      "title": "Troubleshooting HTTP 403 Errors and Wrong Data Visibility in Identity Vault Conditional Access",
      "content_summary": "Addresses HTTP 403 access denials and incorrect data visibility caused by misconfigured conditional access policies or incomplete access reviews.",
      "content_body": "1. Verify the conditional access policy configuration for the affected user group to identify if the block was intentional or a misconfiguration.\n2. Check if an improper access review was recently completed or if pending reviews have lapsed, which often triggers automatic denials or visibility changes.\n3. Confirm that the user's current permissions align with the intended scope of the policy to resolve the 'wrong data' symptom.\n4. Apply the necessary permission updates or policy corrections in Identity Vault to restore appropriate access levels.\n5. Document the change and notify stakeholders once the configuration change has been validated."
